     "xpath": "/html/body/div[1]/div[2]/div/main/div[1]/p[8]"
    },
    "sha256": "f149d227516c265ef970bfe9b3ebd72ad1608a042f2b36be4fb4357697ed130d",
    "text": "Licensure/Certification: In order to become a practicing dentist, students must first obtain licensure. This process includes completing an educational program that is accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA). Students also need to complete Parts I and II of the National Board Dental Examination (NBDE) administered by the Joint Commission on National Dental Examinations. For most U.S. jurisdictions, the last component is that students complete a clinical licensure examination.",
    "url": "https://bulletin.temple.edu/graduate/scd/dentistry/dentistry-dmd/"
   },
   "label": "Licensure/Certification",
   "value": "In order to become a practicing dentist, students must first obtain licensure. This process includes completing an educational program that is accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA). Students also need to complete Parts I and II of the National Board Dental Examination (NBDE) administered by the Joint Commission on National Dental Examinations. For most U.S. jurisdictions, the last component is that students complete a clinical licensure examination."
  },
  {
   "evidence": {
    "locator": {
     "bbox": null,
